WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:05.020
<i>What? Is i7 using Zero's songs
 without his permission?</i>

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.480
<i>Isn't that why Zero got mad 
and graffitied those posters?</i>

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:13.110
Takanashi Productions Special 
Publicity Manager Rokuya Nagi?

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:19.240
I shall turn the buzzing media
 into a flock of sheep.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.250
What's going on?

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.860
Thank you for coming.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.010
I am Takanashi Productions' 
Publicity Manager Rokuya Nagi.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.530
Discover...

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:43.520
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.750
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:51.770
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.110
Wow...

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:07.710
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:12.800
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.550
No matter what tomorrow's 
like, it won't betray us

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:23.270
We'll change even the harshest environments

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:25.940
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.480
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:33.900
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.440
Discover...

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.490
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:44.870
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.250
Night sky

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.390
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:52.590
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:58.180
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:03.790
Wow...

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.160
A-Aren't you Rokuya Nagi-san of IDOLiSH7?

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.510
And now you're a PR manager? Is this a jo—

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:21.740
Quiet, please.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:26.790
The other day, we experienced 
a very sad incident.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.370
Regrettably, that incident created 
several misunderstandings between us

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.360
and the rest of the world.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.510
Today I'd like to take this opportunity

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:40.760
to resolve each and every one 
of those misunderstandings.

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:44.240
There will be a Q&A at the end.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.580
You may ask your questions then.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.390
Who is that guy?

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.500
He's accustomed to making speeches.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.770
Where did he learn to do that?

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.650
That will be all from me.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.610
Now, I will take any questions.

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:03.980
Sir!

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:04.350
Sir!

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:04.840
Sir!

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.880
How do you feel about the 
"Haruki the Betrayer" graffiti?

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:13.290
I am outraged.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:19.340
Haruki transferred the rights to the songs
 he wrote himself to me out of kindness.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:24.860
He hasn't done a single thing 
to deserve to be labeled a traitor.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.320
And of course, neither have we.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.850
Do you have any proof of a formal transfer?

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:34.170
There is a transfer of rights contract 
with both my and Haruki's signatures.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.230
If necessary, I can present it to you.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:38.330
You described the incident as "sad."

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.810
Don't you think there are people 
who are sad that someone

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:42.950
other than Zero is singing 
Sakura Haruki's songs?

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:49.020
Be that as it may, slandering someone
 with graffiti is both childish and a crime.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.710
Were a woman to reject 
my invitation to dinner,

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.960
I certainly would not graffiti 
her home out of sadness.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:59.170
I would improve myself,
 and ask her out again.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:03.470
Though that would require some—
no, a substantial amount of courage.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:07.770
He's good.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:11.700
He won over the reporters 
with grace and humor.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.310
They were all on edge before this started.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.890
Nagicchi's the only one who's mad.

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:17.480
Really?

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.920
He's pretty mad.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.860
He's not smiling with his eyes.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:29.730
Like everyone here, I have great love 
and respect for him and his work.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:35.120
Also, as Haruki's friend and business 
partner, I have affection for him.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:40.740
Additionally, I don't believe Zero himself 
is responsible for these incidents.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:47.390
There's simply no way that a man so beloved
 by all would do something to hurt others.

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:50.520
I hope from the bottom of my heart
 that whoever is behind the graffiti

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:52.900
that caused this disturbance
 is apprehended soon,

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:57.400
and that Zero's honor is restored.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.250
Impressive.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:02.940
He led the conversation towards blaming 
whoever wrote the graffiti instead of Zero.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:07.660
He gave them the impression that Zero 
isn't on the culprit's side, but ours.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.780
This will piss off whoever's responsible.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:14.120
Watch out!

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:24.210
Are you all right?

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.800
Yes. Are you?

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.850
Red spray paint?

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:32.220
How dare they throw something at a woman...

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.420
That's...

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.020
Zero!

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:40.770
Guards, seize that man immediately!

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.610
What? Guards?

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:44.210
Ah, yes, sir!

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.420
Let's go after him, too!

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.480
We'll catch him and beat him to a pulp!

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:49.410
Wait!

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.100
We can't let him hit anyone. After them!

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:51.830
All right!

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.330
We're currently running a campaign.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.830
Would you like one?

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:57.970
Everyone...

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:02.960
Is that...

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:04.210
Zero?

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:05.880
Could it be?

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:22.860
Is that really him?

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:23.960
No way.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:30.950
Zero! Zero! Zero!

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:36.120
<b>It's overflowing!</b>

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:55.780
This song...

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.690
Give me back my song.

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:13.030
That's our song.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.500
Is that really him?

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:18.640
No.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:19.500
Huh?

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:21.830
That's not Zero.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.190
Mitsuki.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:49.570
<b>Will legendary idol Zero 
finally return at the inaugural concert?!</b>

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:49.570
Everyone's saying Zero's going to return 
on the final day of the inaugural concert.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:52.150
Tickets are being sold at high prices.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:55.330
How awful. It's supposed 
to be Re:vale's concert.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:08:00.010
It would certainly be interesting if 
Zero made a comeback at our concert.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:01.190
Right, Momo?

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:04.630
Huh? Yeah. Yeah, it would be.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.340
Are you okay?

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:09.140
Yeah. I think I'll be able to sing today.

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:13.230
Drinking peach-apple juice seems
 to make my throat better.

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:15.840
I received a ton of snacks as gifts, too.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:16.990
Huh?

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:19.360
A letter?

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:21.140
Can I open it?

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.920
I'll do it!

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:25.270
Given the circumstances,
there's no telling what's inside.

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.360
You're overreacting, Okarin.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:30.570
It would be terrible if 
either of you were hurt.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:34.640
What is it?

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:39.540
"If you sing Zero's song at your 
fifth anniversary concert,

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.690
tragedy will befall Zero Arena."

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:45.530
<b>If you sing Zero's song at your fifth anniversary
 concert, tragedy will befall Zero Arena.</b>

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:44.850
It's a threat.

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:49.720
Apparently Re:vale received 
a threatening letter.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.620
They're not sure if it's from a Zero fan.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:58.690
Isn't our agency still getting complaints 
about our singing Sakura Haruki's songs?

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:01.920
Zero's performance hit us hard.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:04.910
I should have performed my own magic.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:05.810
Stop it!

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.570
He's not the real Zero!

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:12.070
Nii-san...

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:15.820
You said the same thing then, too.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.880
Why do you think that?

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:23.190
I can't say exactly why, but when I met Zero,

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:28.080
I felt strangely happy, like a spell 
had been cast on me.

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:31.960
Just a hunch, then? That's not much of a denial.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.150
Why?

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:35.080
Intuition is important.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:40.600
Our experience and knowledge subconsciously 
choose the correct answer.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:45.280
When you don't know the answer on a test, 
it's a good idea to rely on your intuition.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:46.330
Seriously?!

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:49.270
That's odd. I always rely on mine.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:54.540
I fill out my answers with certainty 
instead of relying on intuition.

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:58.500
Who exactly is Zero?

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:02.510
Why did he suddenly vanish and
 then abruptly reappear again?

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:06.610
Everyone in Japan is 
wondering the same thing.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:12.610
<b>Wild Show</b>

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:12.610
<b>Has Zero returned?</b>

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:12.610
<i>Zero suddenly appearing onstage 
at an outdoor concert and—</i>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Has legendary idol Zero finally returned?!</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Economic impact of 100 billion yen over 3 years</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Received high praise from Douglas Rootbank</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>15 years ago</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Suddenly vanished after 
final concert at Zero Arena</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Why did he disappear?</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>According to some in the industry...</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Considering how busy he was at the 
time, it's possible he suddenly fell ill</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>There's a rumor that he had trouble 
with an influential actor</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Tracing the legend</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>What fans have to say about the remodel concert...</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Previous inaugural concert was a solo performance by Zero</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>1 million BD/DVDs sold</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>This year's inaugural concert
 to be "THREE DAYS LIMITED"</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>TRIGGER, Re:vale and IDOLiSH7 
to perform at inaugural concert</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Re:vale announces their intention 
to cover Zero's iconic "Dis one." 
Backlash from Zero fans...</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Rash of graffiti incidents!</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Graffiti on posters around the city...</b>

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>A message to Re:vale? Viral topic on social media</b>

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:15.650
<i>Yeah, I saw him.</i>

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:17.720
Shinbashi

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.720
<i>That was definitely the real Zero.</i>

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.020
Everyone's talking about Zero.

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:21.300
Hey, it's TRIGGER.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.350
Are they headed somewhere?

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:26.220
Shiodome

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:23.200
Turn up the volume.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:26.220
<i>You're in the way. Move, please.</i>

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:29.900
Do you have any comment 
regarding Zero's return?

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:34.100
How do you feel about the other groups 
performing at the inaugural concert?

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:36.070
They're fantastic rivals.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:41.990
Re:vale and IDOLiSH7 are harming 
Zero's image by covering his song and

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.120
singing Sakura Haruki's songs.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.210
Have you met Zero?

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:47.910
Did Zero tell you that?

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.630
Hey, don't intimidate them.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:54.260
A-At the very least, Zero's 
fans aren't happy about it.

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.920
Don't you think it's better 
to leave Zero alone?

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:57.760
Why?

00:10:58.270 --> 00:10:59.550
"Why?"

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.060
I love Zero.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:05.310
I admire him. I wholeheartedly respect him.

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:10.970
But when three modern 
idol groups get together,

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.650
it's hard to believe we can't surpass him.

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:19.330
Tenn-nii...

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:23.950
He provoked them while smiling like an angel.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:27.200
They won't like him for that.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:31.330
Are you trying to say 
you're better than Zero?

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.360
Zero is a legend.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:35.140
What a rude thing to suggest—

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:41.890
I see. Re:vale isn't considered
 legendary yet, and IDOLiSH7 is still new.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:44.620
So you think you have the right to 
speak that rudely about them?

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:49.690
Re:vale and IDOLiSH7 are simply doing 
their best to cover Zero's song

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:51.600
and sing Sakura Haruki's music.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:54.290
It would be different 
if it were Zero himself,

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:57.620
but aren't <i>you </i>embarrassed, trying to lecture
 them when they're doing their best?

00:11:58.130 --> 00:12:01.600
We're simply asking if their actions reflect

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:04.410
a flippant attitude towards a past great idol.

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:06.570
They respect Zero.

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:09.340
That's why they want to get closer 
to him and catch up to him.

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:11.770
You think <i>that's</i> disrespectful?

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:12.600
I—

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:15.570
We're living in the present, not the past.

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:18.920
Don't you want people to 
call this era amazing, too?

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.650
Gaku, you've gone too far.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:27.830
My apologies. Gaku likes both 
Zero and the other groups.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:30.620
That's why he's upset about 
the current situation.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.810
We'll simply do our best to perform

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:36.810
alongside Re:vale and IDOLiSH7 
at the inaugural concert.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:37.850
That's right.

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:43.370
I don't think graffiti or threatening 
letters are part of an idol's job.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:48.120
All we can give to you is this.

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.350
Manager, could you put on some music?

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:50.950
What?

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:52.680
We don't need it.

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:53.910
You want to sing a capella?

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.920
That's fine with me.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:58.170
Wh-What are you...

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:03.670
It's sooner than we planned,
but we're debuting our new song.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:05.990
Hey, wait—

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.190
TRIGGER's new song?!

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:08.370
Get us more time!

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:10.920
Well, what can I really do?

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:13.520
It's a good way to promote the song, anyway.

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:16.380
We're simply a stimulant.

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:18.860
Nothing more, nothing less.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:21.400
But we're supremely exciting.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:24.340
This is TRIGGER's "Last Dimension."

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:33.780
A buzzing area full of Boys & Girl

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:38.630
A flashy jewel in the
 middle of wriggling lust

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:43.080
Hiding in the darkness
 is a dubious silhouette

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:48.200
Who are you? (Yeah, are you kidding me?)

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:53.060
A fuzzy feeling, I can hear the footsteps

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:57.890
The freezing eyes force Attention

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:02.320
A tough approach to curiosity

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:07.820
Who are you? (Yeah, I came to see you)

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:16.790
It's a one-on-one battle, so I can't lose

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:21.590
You forget to even breathe

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:26.360
Hurry up and find out

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:31.790
Moving Moving Moving Moving...

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:35.600
Don't hesitate, Dancing! Amazing!

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:42.060
Aim only for the hope of tomorrow

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:45.180
Now in Dimension, In section

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:51.520
In the gap of dimensions I challenge, 
Last own battle

00:14:51.520 --> 00:15:01.370
I'm not going to go easy on you, 
if our encounter was inevitable

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:10.390
Just try and start something,
now who will be the one

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:16.880
To pull the trigger?

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:44.840
Wow, exciting.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.480
Impressive as always.

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:48.130
They're so cool.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.340
Your brother is amazing.

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:53.860
Yeah. He's so cool...

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:56.010
Please don't fanboy over him.

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:58.010
TRIGGER's good.

00:15:58.010 --> 00:15:59.930
They've got conviction.

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:01.520
They don't hesitate, either.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:04.270
We should follow their lead!

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.220
Let's be true to ourselves. Joy and joy!

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:09.840
Let's enjoy the trouble.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:14.070
Yeah, you're right. Let's focus on 
the success of the concert.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:16.200
We get to sing on the same 
stage Zero performed on.

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:20.280
Let's remember how we felt 
when we first heard about that!

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:22.070
We won't stop until the end.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:25.080
Shiodome

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:25.080
TRIGGER performs new song

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:23.400
Yeah!

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:23.400
Yes!

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:25.420
<i>Thank you, TRIGGER.</i>

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:27.160
<i>You motivated us.</i>

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:32.560
This is convenient for us, too.

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:33.550
What do you mean?

00:16:34.110 --> 00:16:38.280
A major production company that's both
wealthy and influential with the media

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:42.180
will come to the forefront to 
protect those three troublemakers.

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:47.310
I believe the ruler of that castle 
is a confident perfectionist.

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:49.770
He believes he can control public opinion.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:53.530
And I shall control him.

00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:56.360
I won't let him call us useless again.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.500
Those idiots.

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:07.380
Why would they dive headfirst 
into the Zero scandal?

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:11.490
We can't allow TRIGGER to get 
caught up in this stupid fire.

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:12.250
Anesagi!

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:12.880
Yes, sir.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.630
Gather comments from personalities

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:17.760
both within and outside our agency 
and use them to promote Zero Arena.

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:22.940
We'll manipulate the general 
impression of covering Zero's song.

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:30.440
Anesagi-san!

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:35.450
Please take these documents.

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:42.700
It's a list of celebrities with favorable 
opinions on the Zero problem and TRIGGER.

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:46.540
How did you predict the president's strategy?

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:50.860
Image is vital to both 
entertainers and publicity.

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:55.900
Using clean talent when you want to 
convey a clean image is standard.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:58.660
From among those individuals,

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:02.100
I chose those most likely to 
support TRIGGER on this matter.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:07.100
You're a smart girl.

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:09.200
<i>It was Iori-san's suggestion.</i>

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:11.100
<i>And those on the list
 favor not only TRIGGER,</i>

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:13.920
<i>but IDOLiSH7 and Re:vale as well!</i>

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.850
Anesagi-san, Takanashi-san.

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:18.270
Okazaki-san!

00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:20.870
If there's anything I can do, I'll help.

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.240
These idols are putting 
themselves on the line.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:25.860
Let's pour our hearts and souls into making

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:28.160
the Zero Arena inaugural concert a success!

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.780
Of course.

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:31.960
TRIGGER is high-quality, brand-name goods.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.550
I won't let them get a scratch on them.

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:36.280
IDOLiSH7 is the ultimate idol group.

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:38.130
I'll protect them, no matter what!

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:42.550
I'll show you true strength of 
Re:vale, who rose out of nothing.

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:45.610
Well then, let's share a drink.

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:47.610
Actually, I'm too young for—

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:51.560
Idol managers can't go day drinking.

00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:56.280
I meant energy drinks.

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:57.440
Okay!

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:00.110
I'll have some stomach medicine with mine.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.370
Fight... on!

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:12.390
President Yaotome will 
most likely have the media

00:19:12.390 --> 00:19:15.880
aggressively broadcast positive 
comments and news commentary.

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:19.800
<i>Congratulations on Zero Arena's remodel.</i>

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:25.140
<i>Please keep singing Zero's songs at Zero Arena.</i>

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:25.140
<b>Actress</b>

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:25.140
<b>Suga Yoko</b>

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:28.890
<b>Comments from entertainers 
on Zero Arena's remodel</b>

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:30.840
<i>Congratulations on Zero Arena's 
remodel and the inaugural concert.</i>

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:28.890
<b>Actor</b>

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:28.890
<b>Chiba Shizuo</b>

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:35.900
<i>I've known Re:vale's 
Yuki-kun since his debut.</i>

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:42.290
<i>I'm able to sing Zero's songs at 
karaoke since he taught them to me.</i>

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.120
Hey, it's Chiba Shizuo.

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:40.780
The concert at Zero Arena, huh?

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:42.860
Apparently there's some drama over it.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.910
They're being criticized for it. Poor things.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:48.850
What? You went on about how you
 felt sorry for Zero before now.

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:49.620
Really? I did?

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:51.920
Yeah, you definitely did.

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:51.340
All right.

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:56.540
And that press conference will 
be rebroadcast over and over

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.330
with some type of note appended to it.

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:00.950
That press conference?

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:02.710
Rokuya-san's speech.

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:07.180
It's the smartest and most easily 
understood answer to this problem.

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:12.320
<i>Additionally, I don't believe Zero himself 
is responsible for these incidents.</i>

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:15.730
Press conference with
 IDOLiSH7's Rokuya Nagi

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:13.270
They still haven't caught 
whoever did the graffiti?

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:18.560
<i>There's simply no way that a man so beloved
 by all would do something to hurt others.</i>

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:14.500
I guess not.

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:17.930
If Nagi-kun's this insistent, then 
maybe it really was an impostor.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:20.940
Press conference with
 IDOLiSH7's Rokuya Nagi

00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:19.270
Of course it was!

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:21.150
I've been saying that this whole time.

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:24.200
Is that right? I'm excited for the concert.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.750
Jeez.

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:28.200
Good luck, IDOLiSH7.

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:34.580
During this time, Rokuya-san's classy, 
elegant, and clean image will be key.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:38.170
We must be careful to protect his image.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:40.170
Hi, girl.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:44.680
Your beautiful eyes drew me to—oh?

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:47.690
Oh, no!

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:49.820
Nagi-san, please stop the flirting for a while.

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:48.900
Oh?

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:52.890
Your elegant image is 
very important right now.

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:54.390
Okay.

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:55.900
Oh.

00:20:56.930 --> 00:21:00.900
I promise I'll get the Cocona-chan cosplay plan 
approved for <i>Lovely Night With You</i>, okay?

00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:04.400
Wow! Exciting!

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:05.980
Be <i>elegant.</i>

00:21:05.980 --> 00:21:07.410
Okay, girl.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:13.000
By holding our heads high in 
the face of any adversity,

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.480
the rest of us can reassure our fans.

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:16.310
<b><i>Talking Saturday</i></b>

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:18.620
That's our most important job.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:26.030
Hello. We are Re:vale.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:29.050
Let's enjoy another Monday night together.

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:30.520
Thanks for coming.

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:44.940
Thanks for tonight.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:46.860
We've missed you.

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:48.870
Let's keep the energy high until the end!

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.580
Come with us!

00:21:58.350 --> 00:21:59.830
Good evening.

00:22:00.390 --> 00:22:02.130
We're IDOLiSH7.

00:22:05.690 --> 00:22:08.040
Riku-kun, we've been waiting for you!

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:09.430
Thank you.

00:22:09.850 --> 00:22:14.430
There were times we nearly broke down, 
but your voices always supported us.

00:22:17.490 --> 00:22:19.060
So...

00:22:19.840 --> 00:22:21.690
I hope you'll stick with us.

00:22:24.690 --> 00:22:28.880
We promise we'll do our absolute best.

00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:30.450
#12 Ripples

00:22:32.710 --> 00:22:34.820
I'm impressed.

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:37.860
Yaotome-kun knows where and how to advertise.

00:22:37.860 --> 00:22:40.790
The agency has been receiving 
fewer phone calls, too.

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:42.800
He really saved us this time.

00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:43.460
Yeah.

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:46.910
I still can't forgive him 
for the debut single,

00:22:46.910 --> 00:22:48.420
but my opinion of him has improved some.

00:22:49.490 --> 00:22:52.490
Musubi, we'll have to thank him.

00:22:53.610 --> 00:22:56.140
Banri-kun, you must be relieved, too.

00:22:57.290 --> 00:23:00.420
We can't have them coming 
to a standstill here.

00:23:01.040 --> 00:23:06.550
I want our boys... and them
to shine from even greater heights.

00:23:06.550 --> 00:23:07.840
You're right.

00:23:07.840 --> 00:23:11.200
All that's left is for Momo-kun 
to recover his voice.

00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:28.710
Could you not enter my greenroom
 without asking me first?

00:23:29.350 --> 00:23:30.720
Where's Momo-san?

00:23:34.730 --> 00:23:37.220
He doesn't seem to want to be around me.

00:23:37.820 --> 00:23:40.300
Even you get depressed 
like the rest of us, huh?

00:23:43.590 --> 00:23:45.760
I accepted the movie job.

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:48.230
I know. I heard from the director.

00:23:48.520 --> 00:23:50.530
Shizuo-san will be delighted.

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:56.700
His dear son is making
his film debut, after all.

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:56.700
Monthly Kinema

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:56.700
<b>Chiba Shizuo
 Exclusive Interview
"Speaking on the Origin of Acting"</b>

00:23:57.640 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:57.640 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"Lies and Formality"</b>
